            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0690" n="586" xml:id="pg586"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.111/132.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 25, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence on
                    the subject of the alleged activity of Syrians in opposition to the Government
                    of Haiti, and more particularly to Mr. Furniss’s No. 1263, of July 25, 1913, the
                    Department encloses herewith, for your information, a copy of a despatch of
                    September 12, 1913, from the American Consul at Kingston, Jamaica, in this
                    connection.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
